# K23: exact-minimum ambiguous-decomposition boundary exhausts the step budget.
# A 100-byte all-'a' subject against (a{10,20}){10,50} has exactly one valid
# decomposition (10 x 10) but the VM explores the ambiguous space and returns
# RX_ERR_STEPS against the default 1,000,000 budget where python re answers
# instantly. Oracle-verified (python re): span (0,100), group 1 (90,100).
# See docs/dev/known_issues.md K23. From the D27 blinded quantifier corpus.
pattern (a{10,20}){10,50}
m "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa" 0 100
g 1 90 100
